---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro'
import PageLinks from '../../components/PageLinks.astro'
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'select', text: 'SELECT pipeline' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'predicates', text: 'Predicates' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'grouping', text: 'Grouping and aggregates' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'grouping-sets', text: 'ROLLUP, CUBE, and GROUPING SETS' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'ctes-and-subqueries', text: 'CTEs and subqueries' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'sets-and-ordering', text: 'Sets and ordering' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'row-sources', text: 'VALUES, series, and UNNEST' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'files', text: 'Query files' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'explain', text: 'EXPLAIN' },
]
---
<DocsLayout title="Query data" description="Query thinDB with filters, grouping, grouping sets, CTEs, set operations, subqueries, and file scans." headings={headings}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="SQL guide" title="Query data" description="thinDB supports the analytical SQL shapes needed to scan, transform, group, combine, and rank columnar data while keeping execution behavior explicit." />
  <h2 id="select">SELECT pipeline</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT
  customer_id,
  amount * exchange_rate AS converted_amount,
  CASE WHEN amount >= 1000 THEN 'large' ELSE 'standard' END AS band,
  CASE status WHEN 'paid' THEN 1 WHEN 'void' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END AS sign
FROM invoices
WHERE issued_on >= DATE '2026-01-01'
ORDER BY converted_amount DESC
LIMIT 100 OFFSET 20;`} />
  <p>Projection expressions support column references, typed literals, arithmetic, casts, scalar functions, searched and simple <code>CASE</code>, scalar subqueries, session variables, and nested-value access such as <code>arr[1]</code>, <code>m['key']</code>, and <code>s.field</code>. Aliases can be referenced by downstream ordering where unambiguous.</p>

  <h2 id="predicates">Predicates</h2>
  <p>Use <code>=</code>, <code>&lt;&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&gt;=</code>, the null-safe <code>&lt;=&gt;</code> and <code>IS [NOT] DISTINCT FROM</code>, <code>BETWEEN</code>, <code>IN</code>, <code>LIKE</code>, <code>REGEXP</code>/<code>RLIKE</code>, <code>IS NULL</code>, <code>IS NOT NULL</code>, and boolean <code>AND</code>/<code>OR</code>/<code>NOT</code>. Row values compare element-wise, so <code>(a, b) IN ((1, 2), (3, 4))</code> works. SQL three-valued null semantics apply.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT * FROM events
WHERE occurred_at BETWEEN '2026-07-01 00:00:00' AND '2026-07-31 23:59:59'
  AND kind IN ('checkout', 'refund')
  AND source LIKE 'web%'
  AND path REGEXP '^/api/v[0-9]+/'
  AND deleted_at IS NULL;`} />
  <Callout type="note" title="NOT IN with NULLs"><p>A NULL inside a <code>NOT IN</code> list or subquery result is skipped rather than making every comparison unknown, so <code>x NOT IN (1, NULL)</code> is true for <code>x = 2</code>. This differs from standard three-valued logic.</p></Callout>

  <h2 id="grouping">Grouping and aggregates</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT
  customer_id,
  COUNT(*) AS invoice_count,
  COUNT(DISTINCT currency) AS currencies,
  SUM(amount) AS total,
  SUM(amount) FILTER (WHERE status = 'paid') AS paid_total,
  MAX_BY(invoice_id, amount) AS largest_invoice
FROM invoices
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING SUM(amount) > 10000
ORDER BY total DESC
LIMIT 50;`} />
  <p><code>agg(...) FILTER (WHERE condition)</code> aggregates only the rows where the condition is true. Grouping can route through hash, sort, radix, low-cardinality, or partitioned execution based on input shape and memory budget. This physical choice does not reorder the logical query.</p>

  <h2 id="grouping-sets">ROLLUP, CUBE, and GROUPING SETS</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT region, product, SUM(amount) AS total, GROUPING(region, product) AS level
FROM sales
GROUP BY ROLLUP(region, product)
ORDER BY region, product;

SELECT region, channel, COUNT(*)
FROM sales
GROUP BY GROUPING SETS ((region), (channel), ());`} />
  <p><code>GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP</code>, <code>ROLLUP(...)</code>, <code>CUBE(...)</code> (up to 12 columns), <code>GROUPING SETS</code>, and mixes such as <code>GROUP BY a, ROLLUP(b)</code> are supported, up to 4,096 sets. <code>GROUPING()</code> and <code>GROUPING_ID()</code> work in the select list, <code>HAVING</code>, <code>ORDER BY</code>, and <code>CASE</code>. As in MySQL, empty input returns no rows, not a grand-total row.</p>

  <h2 id="ctes-and-subqueries">CTEs and subqueries</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`WITH customer_totals(customer_id, total) AS (
  SELECT customer_id, SUM(amount)
  FROM invoices
  GROUP BY customer_id
), active AS (
  SELECT customer_id FROM customers WHERE status = 'active'
)
SELECT c.customer_id, c.total
FROM customer_totals c
WHERE c.customer_id IN (SELECT customer_id FROM active)
  AND c.total > (SELECT AVG(total) FROM customer_totals);

WITH RECURSIVE ancestry(id, parent_id, depth) AS (
  SELECT id, parent_id, 0 FROM accounts WHERE id = 42
  UNION ALL
  SELECT a.id, a.parent_id, r.depth + 1
  FROM accounts a JOIN ancestry r ON a.id = r.parent_id
)
SELECT * FROM ancestry;`} />
  <p>Supported forms include named CTEs with optional column lists, <code>WITH RECURSIVE</code> (MySQL 8.4 rules), scalar subqueries, <code>IN</code>/<code>NOT IN</code> subqueries, <code>EXISTS</code>/<code>NOT EXISTS</code>, derived tables with column lists (<code>FROM (...) AS d(a, b)</code>), and correlated subqueries. A recursive CTE stops when a step adds no rows, or at a <code>LIMIT</code> on its body.</p>

  <h2 id="sets-and-ordering">Sets and ordering</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT customer_id FROM invoices
UNION
SELECT customer_id FROM refunds
ORDER BY customer_id;

SELECT customer_id FROM invoices
EXCEPT
SELECT customer_id FROM churned;

SELECT * FROM invoices ORDER BY ALL DESC LIMIT 10;`} />
  <p><code>UNION [ALL | DISTINCT]</code>, <code>INTERSECT [DISTINCT]</code>, and <code>EXCEPT [DISTINCT]</code> (also spelled <code>MINUS</code>) combine compatible query outputs. <code>INTERSECT</code> binds tighter than <code>UNION</code> and <code>EXCEPT</code>, and a trailing <code>ORDER BY</code>/<code>LIMIT</code> applies to the whole chain; parenthesize an arm to give it its own. <code>INTERSECT ALL</code> and <code>EXCEPT ALL</code> are rejected.</p>
  <p><code>DISTINCT</code>, multi-column <code>ORDER BY</code>, ordinals, <code>ORDER BY ALL</code> (every select item, left to right), <code>NULLS FIRST</code>/<code>NULLS LAST</code>, <code>LIMIT</code>, <code>OFFSET</code>, and ANSI <code>FETCH FIRST n ROWS ONLY</code> are available.</p>

  <h2 id="row-sources">VALUES, series, and UNNEST</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT * FROM (VALUES (1, 'a'), (2, 'b')) AS v(n, label);

SELECT d.n, DATE '2026-01-01' + INTERVAL d.n MONTH AS month_start
FROM generate_series(0, 11) AS d(n);

SELECT o.order_id, item.sku
FROM orders o, unnest(o.skus) AS item(sku);`} />
  <ul>
    <li><code>VALUES</code> rows and <code>TABLE t</code> stand anywhere a query can: at the top level, in set-operation arms, derived tables, CTE bodies, and subqueries.</li>
    <li><code>generate_series(start, stop[, step])</code> returns one <code>BIGINT</code> column with inclusive bounds. Write it bare or as <code>TABLE(generate_series(...))</code>; arguments may also be named (<code>start =&gt;</code>, <code>end =&gt;</code>, <code>step =&gt;</code>).</li>
    <li><code>unnest(a1[, a2 ...])</code> returns a row per array position, zipping several arrays; NULL and empty arrays produce no rows.</li>
    <li>Both read the <code>FROM</code> items before them (lateral), so they can expand a column of each row.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="files">Query files</h2>
  <p>With <code>--file-root PATH</code>, SQL may scan approved CSV, JSON, and Parquet files under that root through <code>read_csv</code>, <code>read_json</code>, <code>read_parquet</code>, or recognized file sources. Paths outside the configured root are rejected.</p>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`SELECT region, SUM(amount) AS total
FROM read_parquet('imports/invoices.parquet')
GROUP BY region;`} />

  <h2 id="explain">EXPLAIN</h2>
  <CodeBlock language="sql" code={`EXPLAIN SELECT customer_id, SUM(amount)
FROM invoices GROUP BY customer_id;

EXPLAIN (FORMAT JSON) SELECT * FROM invoices WHERE invoice_id = 1001;`} />
  <Callout type="note" title="ANALYZE status"><p><code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> is accepted, but currently aliases plain <code>EXPLAIN</code>; it does not execute the query or report measured row counts and timings.</p></Callout>
  <PageLinks previous={{ label: 'Tables and data', href: '/sql/tables/' }} next={{ label: 'Joins', href: '/sql/joins/' }} />
</DocsLayout>
